{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#114","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#114","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#114\",\"parent_revision\":\"2ccfb3d706a8ea84e812fb968f5beef287c0a1db5bd7aca32a85d0c1e80ce433\",\"root_revision\":\"2ccfb3d706a8ea84e812fb968f5beef287c0a1db5bd7aca32a85d0c1e80ce433\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `packages/skilllint/rules/pl_series.py` \u2014 `MARKETPLACE_JSON_ROOT_KEYS`\\n- `packages/skilllint/plugin_validator.py` \u2014 `_fix_marketplace_json_metadata_keys`, its wiring, the unconditional `can_fix()` call site\\n- `packages/skilllint/tests/test_plugin_structure_validator.py` \u2014 `TestMarketplaceJsonLayout`\\n\\nFull design brief: `.tmp/scratch/solution-design-pl006-marketplace-root-keys.md`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproduction Verified Against The Running Cli\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA `marketplace.json` carrying root-level `description` and `version` \u2014 both documented-valid \u2014 is rewritten by `skilllint check --fix`. The command prints nothing and exits 0. Silent mutation of a valid user file.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Two Causes Compound\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**1. The allowlist is too narrow.** `MARKETPLACE_JSON_ROOT_KEYS` holds only `{metadata, name, owner, plugins}`, so documented root keys are reported as unknown.\\n\\n**2. The \\\"fix\\\" relocates them.** `_fix_marketplace_json_metadata_keys` moves the flagged keys into `metadata` and rebuilds the document from a hardcoded `(\\\"name\\\", \\\"owner\\\", \\\"plugins\\\")` tuple.\\n\\n**Amplifier:** `--fix` calls every validator's `can_fix()` regardless of whether that validator reported anything, so the writer runs on files PL006 never flagged.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Ordering Is Load Bearing\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFix in this order:\\n\\n1. **Delete the relocation auto-fix.** PL006 keeps detecting and reporting a genuinely unknown root key; only the automated repair goes.\\n2. **Then widen the allowlist** to the documented root fields, each key carrying an inline comment naming its source in the vendor doc cache.\\n\\nInverting this causes the data loss it is meant to prevent. `_fix_marketplace_json_metadata_keys` currently raises `NotImplementedError` when any unknown key is present, and that guard is the only thing stopping the hardcoded three-key rebuild from dropping `$schema`, `renames`, and every other unlisted key. Widening the allowlist first removes that guard's coverage and converts a false positive into real data loss.\\n\\nA comment on the constant pointing at the writer would make this coupling discoverable without reading this issue.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Severity Stays Error\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe \\\"unrecognized fields are warnings\\\" line comes from the **plugin.json** reference, not the marketplace one. `packages/skilllint/tests/test_plugin_structure_validator.py` carries captured stderr showing the real marketplace validator emitting `Found 1 error: root: Unrecognized keys`. Downgrading on the wrong document's sentence would itself be an invented constraint.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Already Corrupted Files Are Not Detectable\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`metadata.description` is explicitly valid upstream, so any detection heuristic would be invented. This belongs in the changelog with a `git log -p` pointer rather than in code.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`TestMarketplaceJsonLayout` asserts the exact fix behaviour being deleted; it moves to the new contract rather than losing coverage. The proof is a byte-identity round-trip \u2014 copy a fixture to a temp dir (`--fix` works in place), sha256 before, run `--fix`, `sha256sum -c`. RED first.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"90d1ef2dc0f7038088659bc258574cc7cab0e02a8bd26cbf056b0e977bd9479e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-xlg\"}"}